WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:05.130
"Star Wars" fans got plenty of the things
they expected from the first teaser trailer

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:10.650
for the upcoming "Obi-Wan Kenobi" series,
set to debut on Disney+ in May.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:15.330
Fans have known since August 2019 that Ewan
McGregor would be reprising his role as the

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:19.820
Jedi Master, along with Hayden Christensen's
return as Darth Vader, since the project was

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:21.580
announced a few years ago.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.220
"Hello there!"

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:29.000
However, there were a few surprises in the
"Obi-Wan Kenobi" trailer some fans never expected.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.920
Chief among them were the appearance of the
Inquisitors.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:36.550
The Inquisitors are an order of Force-sensitive
hunters that were trained by Darth Vader in

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:41.140
order to capture, kill, or corrupt any surviving
Jedi in the galaxy.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:46.110
Many of them appear in "Star Wars" series,
like "Star Wars: Rebels," as well as various

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:50.840
related comics and video games, like "Star
Wars: Jedi Fallen Order."

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:54.800
Despite their popularity as villains, this
is the first time that they have appeared

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:59.760
in a live-action context, similar to Cad Bane's
appearance on "The Book of Boba Fett."

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:05.269
However, not every "Star Wars" fan who watched
"Rebels" is jumping for joy at the Inquisitors'

00:01:05.269 --> 00:01:07.049
live-action debut.

00:01:07.049 --> 00:01:11.719
In fact, it's the appearance of the Grand
Inquisitor that has some fans scratching their

00:01:11.719 --> 00:01:12.819
heads.

00:01:12.819 --> 00:01:17.729
Fans on Reddit made it clear that this live-action
Grand Inquisitor was close to the version

00:01:17.729 --> 00:01:22.429
of the character we see in "Star Wars: Rebels,"
but didn't quite look right.

00:01:22.429 --> 00:01:23.429
One user wrote,

00:01:23.429 --> 00:01:27.979
"I realize the 'Rebels' style is a cartoonified,
stretched-out look.

00:01:27.979 --> 00:01:31.799
But even so, I would have preferred him look
a little thinner in the face."

00:01:31.799 --> 00:01:32.950
Another user observed,

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:37.369
"He definitely looks less slim than I thought
he'd look in live-action."

00:01:37.369 --> 00:01:38.849
Another responded that,

00:01:38.849 --> 00:01:43.079
"In 'Rebels,' he gives off the air of a diffident,
aristocratic fencer.

00:01:43.079 --> 00:01:44.829
I'm not getting that vibe from him.

00:01:44.829 --> 00:01:46.439
He looks like a haunted house reject."

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:52.499
It is worth noting that the Grand Inquisitor's
species, the Pau'ans are notoriously slim,

00:01:52.499 --> 00:01:54.469
and this character is no exception.

00:01:54.469 --> 00:01:59.880
In "Rebels," he is depicted as noticeably
taller and thinner than the majority of characters.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:05.079
Previous live-action depictions of the Pau'an
species are also extremely slim.

00:02:05.079 --> 00:02:06.389
One Reddit poster wrote,

00:02:06.389 --> 00:02:08.250
"First thing I noticed as well.

00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:09.920
Aren't their heads a little longer too?

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:13.600
He didn't look much like the Pau'ans from
'Revenge of The Sith' in my opinion."

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:18.830
This, of course, doesn't mean that this new
portrayal should be automatically discounted.

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:23.811
Cad Bane's appearance in "The Book of Boba
Fett" also led to some minor fan outcry, but

00:02:23.811 --> 00:02:27.430
was overall well-liked by at least a portion
of the viewing audience.

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:31.090
"Consider this my final lesson.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:34.800
Look out for yourself."

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:39.040
Now that we've seen what the "Obi-Wan Kenobi"
version of the Grand Inquisitor will look

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:44.200
like, it's important to go over who exactly
the Inquisitors are in the world of "Star

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.200
Wars."

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:49.370
As we mentioned, they are an order of Jedi
hunters trained by Darth Vader to assist him

00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:52.590
in the Jedi Purge following the events of
Order 66.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:57.830
While their exact numbers aren't well-known,
quite a few make appearances in "Rebels" and

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:58.960
other media.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:03:03.360
Putting aside the Grand Inquisitor, one of
the other Inquisitors we see rendered in live-action

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:07.650
for the very first time is the Fifth Brother,
played by Sung Kang.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:12.140
He is the helmet-sporting gentleman leading
a squad of Stormtroopers at the 1-minute,

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:13.970
15-second mark in the teaser trailer.

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:18.750
He's also one of the several Inquisitors to
make multiple appearances in "Rebels."

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:23.770
Another is Reva, a brand new Inquisitor whose
story is, thus far, unknown.

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:28.520
Considering that she hasn't yet made an appearance
in any other Star Wars media, her fate is

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.460
the most ambiguous of the characters we've
seen in the trailer.

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:36.640
Then, of course, there's the Grand Inquisitor,
the leader of the bunch who terrorized Kanan

00:03:36.640 --> 00:03:40.540
Jarrus and Ezra Bridger on multiple occasions
in "Rebels."

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:45.550
A former Jedi, the Grand Inquisitor is about
as dangerous as the Empire gets without Vader

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:46.590
getting involved.

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:51.460
In other words, his involvement in the events
of "Obi-Wan Kenobi" spells big trouble for

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:54.600
both Obi-Wan and the young Luke Skywalker.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:58.660
Thankfully, that intimidating presence is
present in the show's trailer.

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:02.370
We'll just have to wait and see whether or
not the fans will be able to overcome his

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:04.150
new look.

